| `dom` draws in a browser, and this is not one. Every handler answers an
| Exception rather than pretending to draw — an application drawing into
| nothing is a mistake worth naming, not a page that happened to be empty.
|
| The module is linkable here anyway, so one application can be built both
| ways and ask `Linked` which it is. The half that can actually draw is a
| `.a` linked into a `--target wasm` build; nothing in this suite is one.

link "native_modules/dom.so" as dom

emit Render { into = "#app", tree = { tag = "p", children = ["hi"] } } to dom get r
assert r ∈ Exception
assert r.source = "dom"

emit Style { css = "p { color: red }" } to dom get s
assert s ∈ Exception

| A class it does not handle is null, not an error: the particle may have
| been meant for something else entirely.
emit Whatever {} to dom get other
assert other = null
